/-!
# Unicode Bidirectional Algorithm (UAX #9): a pure, total port of unicode-bidi 0.3.18

usvg lays out mixed-direction text with the Rust crate `unicode-bidi` 0.3.18
(`BidiInfo::new(text, Some(level))`, then `visual_runs(para, para.range)`),
and shapes each run with harfrust, which mirrors brackets etc. in RTL runs.
This module reproduces those results exactly, codepoint by codepoint:

* `bidiClass`  — the crate's `Bidi_Class` table (Unicode 16.0.0; unlisted
  codepoints are `L`, as in the crate).
* `paragraphLevels` — the crate's `BidiInfo.levels`: P3 is replaced by the
  caller's explicit paragraph level, then X1–X8 (directional status stack of
  depth 125, with the "Retaining Explicit Formatting Characters" variant the
  crate implements: X9-removed characters keep a level and class `BN`), X10
  (isolating run sequences with the crate's `sos`/`eos` choices), W1–W7,
  N0 (BD16 bracket pairs, 63-entry stack, canonical-equivalent brackets
  U+2329/U+232A ≡ U+3008/U+3009), N1–N2, I1–I2, and finally the crate's
  `assign_levels_to_removed_chars` (each X9-removed character takes the
  level of the character before it).
* `levels`     — `reordered_levels` for one line spanning the whole text:
  L1 (trailing whitespace and isolate controls, and segment/paragraph
  separators with the whitespace before them, reset to the paragraph level;
  X9-removed characters take the level of the character before them).
* `visualRuns` — L2 as `visual_runs` returns it: maximal same-level runs in
  visual order. L3 (combining marks) and L4 (mirroring) are not applied here,
  as in the crate; `mirror` provides harfrust's `Bidi_Mirroring_Glyph` for
  the caller's L4.

The crate works on UTF-8 byte offsets; everything here is per codepoint. The
crate's byte-level loops give every byte of a character the same class and
level, so the per-codepoint formulation computes the same result. The crate's
departures from the letter of UAX #9 are reproduced on purpose, e.g.:
`iter_backwards_from` walks earlier level runs of a sequence *forwards*
(`backScan`, used by N0's preceding-strong search and the BN clean-ups);
X5c only looks at the innermost open isolate; a BD16 stack overflow only
abandons the rest of the current level run; the last level run's `eos` is the
paragraph direction when the last non-removed character *before its end in the
text* is an isolate initiator; the N0 embedding direction is the level of the
sequence's first character even when X9 removes it.

**Paragraphs.** The whole input is treated as ONE paragraph, even if it
contains a paragraph separator (class `B`, e.g. U+2029 or `\n`): a `B` inside
the text behaves as in the crate's single-paragraph `ParagraphBidiInfo`
(level = paragraph level, neutral in N1, reset by L1), and the FSI
look-ahead / isolate matching do not stop at it. `BidiInfo::new` would split
the text there instead; usvg only reads `paragraphs[0]`, and its text chunks
never contain `B`, so the two agree on every input usvg produces.

Every loop is a `for` over a range bounded by the input size or a constant;
the only super-linear parts are the W4 look-ahead and N0 bracket scans, which
are bounded by the square of the input length (as in the crate).
-/

namespace LeanSvg.Bidi

/-! ## Bidi classes -/

/-- `Bidi_Class` values (UAX #9 table 4). The constructor order is the one the
generated table below uses. -/
inductive Cls where
  | L | R | AL | EN | ES | ET | AN | CS | NSM | BN | B | S | WS | ON
  | LRE | LRO | RLE | RLO | PDF | LRI | RLI | FSI | PDI
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr, Inhabited, BEq

/-- The class with table index `k` (constructor order), `L` if out of range. -/
def clsOfIndex (k : Nat) : Cls :=
  #[Cls.L, .R, .AL, .EN, .ES, .ET, .AN, .CS, .NSM, .BN, .B, .S, .WS, .ON,
    .LRE, .LRO, .RLE, .RLO, .PDF, .LRI, .RLI, .FSI, .PDI].getD k .L

/-- Removed by rule X9 (the crate's `removed_by_x9`). -/
def removedX9 : Cls → Bool
  | .RLE | .LRE | .RLO | .LRO | .PDF | .BN => true
  | _ => false

/-- Isolate initiator (`RLI`, `LRI`, `FSI`). -/
def isIsoInit : Cls → Bool
  | .RLI | .LRI | .FSI => true
  | _ => false

/-- Neutral or isolate formatting character (`NI` in UAX #9). -/
def isNI : Cls → Bool
  | .B | .S | .WS | .ON | .FSI | .LRI | .RLI | .PDI => true
  | _ => false

/-- The embedding direction of a level: `L` for even, `R` for odd. -/
def levelCls (l : Nat) : Cls := if l % 2 == 0 then .L else .R

